    "slug": "between-two-hills",
    "artist": 1,
    "category": 5,
    "image": "artworks/40321359152354068.jfif",
    "short_description": "A tactile mixed-media work exploring migration, belonging and the spaces that exist between home and elsewhere.",
    "description": "Between Two Hills combines fragments of fabric, handwritten marks, acrylic paint and found paper. The layered construction reflects the artist's interest in personal histories and the physical objects people carry between places. Stitching becomes both a structural element and a visual metaphor for connection, repair and belonging.",
